@startuml
title Diagrama de Secuencia - Editar Aula (CLI HTTP)

actor "Administrador" as Admin
participant "CLI (Click)" as CLI
participant "APIClient" as Client
participant "API (FastAPI)" as API
participant "AulaService" as Service
participant "AulaRepository" as Repo
database "Base de Datos" as DB

Admin -> CLI: Ejecuta 'sighor aulas edit 5'
activate CLI
CLI -> Client: get('/aulas/5')
activate Client
Client -> API: GET /aulas/5 (Bearer Token)
activate API
API -> Service: obtener_aula(5)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: get_by_id(5)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: SELECT * FROM aulas WHERE id = 5
activate DB
DB --> Repo: Aula existente
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Aula
deactivate Repo
Service --> API: AulaResponse
deactivate Service
API --> Client: 200 OK (Aula JSON)
deactivate API
Client --> CLI: aula_actual
deactivate Client
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Nuevo nombre? [actual: {nombre}]
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa nuevo nombre (o Enter para mantener)
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Nueva capacidad? [actual: {capacidad}]
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa nueva capacidad
CLI -> Admin: Prompt: Nuevo edificio? [actual: {edificio}]
Admin -> CLI: Ingresa nuevo edificio
CLI -> Client: put('/aulas/5', data={campos_modificados})
activate Client
Client -> API: PUT /aulas/5 (AulaUpdate JSON + Bearer Token)
activate API
API -> Service: editar_aula(5, aula_update)
activate Service
Service -> Repo: update(5, aula_update)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB: UPDATE aulas SET ... WHERE id = 5
activate DB
DB --> Repo: OK
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service: Aula actualizada
deactivate Repo
Service --> API: AulaResponse
deactivate Service
API --> Client: 200 OK (Aula JSON)
deactivate API
Client --> CLI: Response(200, aula_json)
deactivate Client
CLI --> Admin: Aula actualizada exitosamente
deactivate CLI

note right of API
  **Backend FastAPI reutilizado:**
  - AulaService
  - AulaRepository
  - Validación Pydantic (AulaUpdate)
  Sin modificaciones
end note

@enduml
